// Named weathers (crates/terra_world/src/weather.rs, docs/weather.md, D418): what each name
// means, as the least of each quantity, for a run to find a moment (`--weather snowfall`), a
// forecast to name one and people to talk about. The weather is the climate's (`climate.ron`),
// and everything drawn reads its quantities; a named weather changes only the grade, its own.
//
//   cloud      cloud at least, 0 to 1
//   rain_mm_h  rain at least, millimetres an hour
//   snow_mm_h  snow at least, as its water, millimetres an hour (a millimetre is about a
//              centimetre of fresh snow)
//   wind_m_s   wind at least, metres a second
//   grade      the grade while it holds (D419), over the neutral one (D370): white balance as
//              Bevy takes it (temperature below 0 toward blue, tint above 0 toward magenta, which
//              keeps a cold balance off cyan) and saturation as a share. A heavier weather with no
//              grade of its own takes the last listed one it also is.
//
// snow_lying_opens_ev  stops the camera opens with the ground round the eye under snow, scaled
//              by how much of it is (D419: "Yes, about +0.5 EV"), so snow reads white, not
//              grey; bare ground, so summer and every weather without snow on the ground, keeps
//              its exposure.
(
named: [
    (name: "overcast", cloud: 0.95),
    (name: "rain", cloud: 0.95, rain_mm_h: 0.5),
    (name: "heavy rain", cloud: 0.95, rain_mm_h: 2.0),
    (name: "storm", cloud: 0.95, rain_mm_h: 4.0, wind_m_s: 9.0),
    // Snow falling grades cool, as the developers chose from side-by-side stills ("Cool").
    (name: "snowfall", cloud: 0.95, snow_mm_h: 0.8,
        grade: Some((temperature: -0.05, tint: 0.05, saturation: 0.9))),
    (name: "heavy snow", cloud: 0.95, snow_mm_h: 1.8),
    (name: "blizzard", cloud: 0.95, snow_mm_h: 1.2, wind_m_s: 9.0),
],
snow_lying_opens_ev: 0.5,
)
